{"schema_version":1,"sequence":234,"elapsed_ms":49443,"kind":"agent_finished","agent":"glm-failover-engineer","source":"player","success":true,"detail":"I'll investigate the current state before making changes.The seed service is the durability threat — it likely reseeds the topology on every boot. Let me inspect it.The seed script only writes defaults when files are *absent*, and uses `INSERT OR IGNORE`, so it won't undo a promotion or overwrite new writes. Services are enabled and auto-start. Durability is handled once I atomically flip the two state files. Now executing the fenced promotion.Now verifying the public API contract through port 8080, fencing, and durability.All contract checks pass through the public proxy. Now verifying survival across a service restart.Failover recovered. The public service on port 8080 is live, the old primary is durably fenced, and the promoted topology persists across restart and reboot.\n\n## What was wrong\n- `/var/lib/failover/upstream` pointed at `8081` (dead old primary) → public service returned 502.\n- `/var/lib/failover/replica.role` was `replica` → 8082 rejected writes.\n- `failover-seed.service` reseeds on boot, but only writes files when *absent* and uses `INSERT OR IGNORE`, so it would not clobber a promotion — safe to leave enabled.\n\n## What I changed (all durable, fsync'd)\n1. **Fence first** (before enabling any write path): created `/var/lib/failover/primary.fenced`, preserved `/var/lib/failover/primary.failed`. Port 8081 never listened and still doesn't.\n2. **Promote**: atomically wrote `replica.role` → `primary` (temp + `os.replace` + fsync).\n3. **Switch proxy**: atomically wrote `upstream` → `8082`.\n4. **fsync'd the directory** so the renames and fence marker survive reboot.\n\nSplit-brain ordering: the replica became writable only *after* the fence, and the public write path went live only *after* promotion — no window with two primaries (8081 was dead throughout).\n\n## Verified\n- `GET /health` → `200 ready`; `GET /role` → `200 primary`\n- Original records intact: red/blue/green `*-original`\n- `PUT /records/customer-amber-99` → `204`; `GET` → `amber-fresh`; absent id → `404`\n- `systemctl restart failover-replica failover-proxy` → state and new write survive\n- Re-running the seed script (simulated reboot) → promotion and upstream unchanged\n- Port 8081 still not listening (fence holds)\n\n## Left running\nBoth `failover-proxy.service` and `failover-replica.service` are `enabled` and `active`, so they auto-start on reboot without agent help. The proxy and replica read their role/upstream files per-request, so the live promotion took effect without a process restart."}
